{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Has gored three times.</b> That is, three gorings (Mekhilta)." "<b>And has been warned through its owners.</b> A term of warning through witnesses, as in ״הָעֵד הֵעִד בָּנוּ הָאִישׁ״ (Genesis 43)." "<b>And it kills a man, etc.</b> Since it says ״כִּי יִגַּח״ — I have only that it killed him by goring. From where do I learn [liability if] it killed him by biting, by pushing, by kicking? Scripture teaches by saying ״וְהֵמִית״." "<b>Also its owner shall be put to death.</b> By the hand of Heaven. Might one think by the hand of man? Scripture teaches by saying ״מוֹת יוּמַת הַמַּכֶּה״ — 'he is a murderer' — for his own murder you execute him, but you do not execute him for the murder of his ox (Sanhedrin 15)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:43.457099040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}